{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/825575-alternate-ways-to-become-a-changeling","id":825575,"title":"Alternate Ways To Become A Changeling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-07T13:55:52-08:00","id":825575,"title":"Alternate Ways To Become A Changeling?","content":"I'm well aware that the whole abduction, enslavement and escape is fundamental to the game, but hear me out.<br /> <br /> I have talked with Arc about the distinction between Titles in Realm form and Domains regarding the True Fae. The latter is more or less the mythical modus operandi of each Stranger, and apparently a mortal that gets too caught up in such a tale can become a changeling, even if the Other in question has no Titles currently invested into a Realm. That would explain why Nergal from Autumn Nightmares managed to turn Grandfather Thunder from the 1ED Core's section on Miami into a changeling, despite being a free-roaming storm god. Arc, if you're reading this and I'm mistaken about any of this hypothesizing, please correct me.<br /> <br /> The impression I got was that people became changelings in Arcadia because the Wyrd is a LOT more thickly woven into reality there. But isn't the Wyrd nigh-omnipresent? Why can't it become thickly woven in other places?<br /> <br /> What if instead of a Keeper, a child who gets lost in the Hedge is raised by a hobgoblin merchant and the community of other hobs in the Hedge Town? The child is still breaking bread with, working for and learning from fae.<br /> <br /> How about someone who is curious about what inspired the local myths of faerie forts, and finds a glade where the Hedge overlaps with the mortal world at just the right time of the year? They could drink from the divinely crystalline water and be compelled to sleep for a long time, Rip Van Winkle-style. While dormant, they wander for a time beyond time in the Skein, interacting with changelings, incubi, mages and even True Fae. His wandering soul is replaced bit by bit with pieces of the Wyrd, and when he comes to, his body hasn't aged, but has acquired a Mien. Technically, he never even entered the Hedge, and made no deals with a True Fae to survive.<br /> <br /> A person from a rich but eccentric family line that's known for making business and maybe love with odd folk (i.e. multiple types of fae) inherits a shop from an uncle who disappears shortly after with a cryptic explanation. As the heir explores the shop and tries to make sense of the wondrous and terrible things the products do, he discovers that a similar shop opens soon after his. The owner of the rival shop is a Gentry in disguise with a vendetta against the heir's family, and the monster is looking to drive the heir out of business. The Gentry occasionally leaves the shop to avoid suspicion, but can stay there indefinitely because it's a Fair Haven. The heir is not under the Gentry's thumb, but they are struggling against each other as if in a Feud for Titles. That type of close interaction with a Gentry might be enough to turn the heir into a changeling.<br /> <br /> Who knows, maybe Medraut, the Aeon of the Fate Arcanum from Imperial Mysteries, is willing to mimic an Entities spell to turn a mortal into a changeling. It could be a punishment, or it could be a reward.<br /> <br /> Discussing how these changelings would earn Seemings, be impersonated by Fetches and pursued Huntsmen would be fun, methinks. Even if they start with no Seeming, Arc said that there might be room for post-Durance ways to earn one in a supplement, so I'm crossing my fingers. I'd be very glad if the 2ED supplement for the Hedge also suggested alternate ways to become a changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-07-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:08:29-08:00","id":825582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/825575-alternate-ways-to-become-a-changeling#post825575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if instead of a Keeper, a child who gets lost in the Hedge is raised by a hobgoblin merchant and the community of other hobs in the Hedge Town? The child is still breaking bread with, working for and learning from fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the hobgoblins taught him how to make Contracts and Dreamwalk, I'd say this would work. His Kith would likely be something related to his job in the market. However, unless he had a bad experience that made him escape back to the real world, he'd be Seemingless. He also wouldn't really have any reason to leave the Hedge, which would make him difficult to play in a game. He also wouldn't have a Fetch and wouldn't get Huntsmen after him unless he catches the eye of a covetous True Fae that wants him for being such an oddity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/825575-alternate-ways-to-become-a-changeling#post825575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about someone who is curious about what inspired the local myths of faerie forts, and finds a glade where the Hedge overlaps with the mortal world at just the right time of the year? They could drink from the divinely crystalline water and be compelled to sleep for a long time, Rip Van Winkle-style. While dormant, they wander for a time beyond time in the Skein, interacting with changelings, incubi, mages and even True Fae. His wandering soul is replaced bit by bit with pieces of the Wyrd, and when he comes to, his body hasn't aged, but has acquired a Mien. Technically, he never even entered the Hedge, and made no deals with a True Fae to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this would engender a Changeling. How would he know how to make Contracts? Or enter the Hedge? He not only wouldn't have a Seeming, he also wouldn't have a Kith. IMO he'd be fey-related a minor template, like a &quot;Dreamwalker.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/825575-alternate-ways-to-become-a-changeling#post825575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A person from a rich but eccentric family line that's known for making business and maybe love with odd folk (i.e. multiple types of fae) inherits a shop from an uncle who disappears shortly after with a cryptic explanation. As the heir explores the shop and tries to make sense of the wondrous and terrible things the products do, he discovers that a similar shop opens soon after his. The owner of the rival shop is a Gentry in disguise with a vendetta against the heir's family, and the monster is looking to drive the heir out of business. The Gentry occasionally leaves the shop to avoid suspicion, but can stay there indefinitely because it's a Fair Haven. The heir is not under the Gentry's thumb, but they are struggling against each other as if in a Feud for Titles. That type of close interaction with a Gentry might be enough to turn the heir into a changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the character would need to learn how to make Contracts, Dreamwalk and enter the Hedge. He would also not have a Seeming or Kith, since the conditions are not in place for them to get one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/825575-alternate-ways-to-become-a-changeling#post825575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discussing how these changelings would earn Seemings, be impersonated by Fetches and pursued Huntsmen would be fun, methinks. Even if they start with no Seeming, Arc said that there might be room for post-Durance ways to earn one, so I'm crossing my fingers. I'd be very glad if the 2ED supplement for the Hedge also suggested alternate ways to become a changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say my personal favourite way to become a changeling would be a Fae-Touched that never stops looking for their loved one, even if they miss each other in the Hedge and the changeling successfully escapes (what can I say? I'm a sucker for that minor template). Imagine the Fae-Touched mother relentlessly looking for her child. Her sanity falters, her soul is frayed, and she starts talking to the world around her, inadvertently making contracts with things to survive and find her way to her child. She gains a Kith that reflects either her nature (Truefriend, perhaps), or her travel (if her journey takes her through a snow-themed Hedge, she may become a Snowskin). She learns the ways of the Hedge and the way of Dreams, and eventually makes it out, gaining a Seeming. She doesn't have a Fetch and she might never have a Huntsman sent for her unless she catches the eye of a True Fae, but she's still a changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:08:37-08:00","id":825583,"title":"","content":"It would make sense. A lot of real-world stories about faeries and other otherworldly beings say that just interacting with them can permanently change you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:25:30-08:00","id":825592,"title":"","content":"Becoming a changeling involves becoming bound to a being of godlike power over the Wyrd. The True Fae:<br /> <br /> 1. Are the established specimens of such beings (and they're interconnected to boot).<br /> 2. Are at their most potent in their own domains, where the Wyrd is at its most chaotic and malleable.<br /> 3. Are quite prepared to wipe out or permanently hobble any Hedge-born specimens of such that don't somehow go on to become Fae.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd is thickly woven in Arcadia because Arcadia is all the places where the Wyrd is thickly woven and sympathy is a thing. Arcadia is also the place from which the Fae are born, live, and prefer to die. The Wyrd is nigh-omnipresent, yes, but so is the Divine Fire and the God-Machine and the resonance of the Shadow, not a single one of which is any less subject to the demands of hitting a critical mass to accomplish significant feats like utterly changing something into a supernatural being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:27:29-08:00","id":825593,"title":"","content":"Whether or not it'd make a person a changeling, I'd certainly be interested in reading a story of a person being raised/taught by a goblin merchant and becoming one himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:32:05-08:00","id":825598,"title":"","content":"The big thing, I think, is that any way of becoming a Changeling needs to involve the Wyrd, but from a story perspective, I think it should also involve a heavy layer of <i>I will not go back</i>(or, to use the example Shadow gives, <i>They will not go back</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T00:03:29-07:00","id":866290,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking of another alternative to becoming a Changeling that's based on Changelings in Dresden Files, Halflings in the 1E fan supplement Goblin Chronicles, and Changelings in (O)WoD. Basically, you are someone who's born Faetouched, perhaps as the child of another Faetouched or the rare child of two Changelings. You could go your whole (short) life as a normal person. But you risk becoming a Changeling if you are exposed to fae magic later in life. (and let's not forget how attractive you probably will be to the Gentry.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T12:20:16-07:00","id":866485,"title":"","content":"I think a human who spent too much time, especially as a child, in the hedge, would become a hobgoblin or a humaniod hedge beast companion eventually.<br /> <br /> Making someone a Changeling without Arcadia would either require something of GREAT power and sacrifice or already being a being that is part Fae and part mortal going in a quest.<br /> <br /> So a Fetch, Cambion, Incubus, or Fae Touched could go on a quest within the hedge and by the end of the quest the character has managed to become a full Changeling, with a Kith and Seeming.<br /> <br /> Alternately one of these said being gets access to a magic that allows them to inherit or steal the Changeling Template. Example a Echo that allows a Fetch to steal their Changeling's template and soul if they kill their Changeling in a certain way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}